    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry Fitzgerald McCreery are delighted to present to market Number 8 Cedar Crescent, Parcnagowan. A commanding and impressive four bedroom detached family home which has been maintained to the highest standards throughout. \n\nParcnagowan is a popular development of spacious family homes built by McCorry Homes. The location on the Outrath Road, just off the main Waterford Road, is one of the city's most sought-after residential locations. \n\nThe spacious and bright accommodation is provided over two levels and extends to 145.77 sq. m./1,570 sq. ft. The layout at ground floor level comprises a welcoming entrance hall, hot press, guest wc, living room with a feature bay window, open plan kitchen/dining room, utility room and a modern office/ playroom. The layout at first floor level comprises: landing area, four generously sized bedrooms (master with en-suite) and a family bathroom. \n\nLOCATION:\nParcnagowan is located on the Outrath Road, just off the main Waterford Road which is renowned for its convenient location on the edge of Kilkenny City. There are several excellent primary and secondary schools in walking distance including Kilkenny School Project National School in Springfield, Waterford Road, St John of God National School Upper New Street and the De La Salle Boys National Schools a short distance away. Gaelscoil Osrai on Outrath Road, The presentation Secondary School in Loughboy and St Kieran's College on College Road. The property is a short walk to Lidl and Aldi on Waterford Road and SuperValu in Loughboy Shopping Centre. There are a number of childcare facilities within close proximity. A ten-minute walk via the Kells Road will take you into Kilkenny City Centre with its superb choice of restaurants, pubs, coffee houses, boutiques, shops, two shopping centres and the stunning Kilkenny Castle. There are a vast range of amenities practically on the doorstep of this wonderful home.\n\nViewing is highly advised.\n\nFront and Rear Garden:\n\nThe front garden is bordered by a neat hedge on both sides providing ample privacy. A cobblelock driveway provides off-street parking for two cars whilst the property is wired with a Zappi electric car charger. Dual entrance gates allow access to both sides and rear of the property.\n\nThe south facing rear garden is fully enclosed and largely laid in lawn, providing plenty of space for the whole family to enjoy. A large steel garden shed provides additional storage."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 5.45m x 2.16m\nA green painted front door with glass side panel opens into the warm and welcoming entrance hall. Decorative tiled floor and carpeted stairs. Access to alarm panel.\n\nLiving Room - 4.61m x 3.88m + 2.18m x 0.87m\nThis bright and spacious living room is finished to a very high standard and incorporates an impressive bay window overlooking the front garden. A centrally located striking white marble fireplace accommodates a solid fuel stove, which is further complimented by a black marble hearth and decorative surround. The room is finished with solid timber floors and plastered and painted walls, creating the perfect atmosphere for evening relaxation.\n\nGuest WC - 1.62m x 1.43m\nComprising wc and a wash hand basin with fitted vanity underneath. Fully tiled floor, decorative wall paneling and wallpaper. Extractor fan.\n\nKitchen Dining Room - 6.11m x 3.69m + 3.23m x 3.01m\nSpacious and bright open plan kitchen/ dining area presented in immaculate condition and benefitting from triple aspect which floods the space with natural light. The kitchen area is fitted with Shaker-style wall and floor units with marble effect countertops and backsplash. Integrated appliances include dishwasher, a Neff 4 ring hob with impressive extractor fan overhead and Electrolux double oven. The space accommodates a centrally located kitchen island perfect for entertaining. Impressive Golden Age decorative tiling runs through this room, whilst recessed lighting completes this space.\n\nUtility Room - 2.33m x 1.63m\nFitted with Shaker-style cabinetry. Plumbing in place for washing machine and tumble dryer. Tiled floor and plastered and painted walls. A PVC glass panel door gives access to the side of the property.\n\nOffice/ Playroom - 3.23m x 2.93m\nDual aspect office/ playroom overlooking the rear garden. Solid wood herringbone floors and recessed spotlights add to this room's ambience.\n\nLanding - 3.62m x 2.90m\nBright and spacious area with large picture gable end window. Fitted carpet.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.09m x 2.43m\nA well-appointed double room positioned to the front of the property. Complete with fitted carpets, and integrated wardrobes.\n\nMaster Bedroom - 3.97m x 3.05m + 2.15m x 0.89m\nThe master bedroom comprises a spacious double bedroom with a feature bay window overlooking the front of the property. Built in wardrobes and fitted carpet.\n\nEnsuite - 2.39m x 0.97m\nComprising wc, wash hand basin and enclosed shower cubicle with bifold door and Triton T90xr electric shower. Fully tiled walls and floor. Gable end window.\n\nMain Bathroom - 2.37m x 1.74m\nComprising wc, wash hand basin with fitted vanity unit underneath and a stand in bath. Fully tiled walls and floor. Picture window provides natural light.\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.67m x 3.08m\nA double room located to the rear finished with built-in wardrobes, dressing table and fitted carpet.\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.09m x 2.66m\nA bright and spacious double room positioned to the front of the property. Fitted carpet and built in wardrobes.\n\n"
      },
